Overlay patch 0059: the rear-view pane's OPPOSITE-DIRECTION course section
list (VR R16-C step 4; docs/vr-r16-diagnosis/rear-pane.md Q2 option A).

MK64 draws its course as ONE DISPLAY LIST PER (SECTION, CARDINAL DIRECTION):
render_track_sections buckets `camera->rot[1]` into NORTH/EAST/SOUTH/WEST and
emits `addr[(index - 1) * 4 + direction]`. The VR rear-view pane is a third
interpreter walk over the SAME command list (trap D32 -- one list, three
walks), so it inherits the FORWARD camera's yaw quadrant and replays "section
S as seen looking NORTH" while showing you the view looking SOUTH. The
geometry genuinely behind the kart was never in the list at all, and R15's
red control proved that is what the grey band is: drop MK64's below-horizon
ground fill (`vr set rearfloor 0`) and the same band goes BLACK, because there
is nothing behind it.

The game already ships the list we want. Its four direction variants of a
section are in the same table, and the SOUTH one is precisely what MK64 emits
itself whenever the player holds C-left, because `LookBehindCamera`'s rot[1]
is the opposite quadrant. So this patch emits it, bracketed:

    G_NOOP 0x62      <- eyes-only span begins
    gSPDisplayList(addr[(index-1)*4 + direction])          (unchanged)
    G_NOOP 0x63
    G_NOOP 0x64      <- rear-only span begins
    gSPDisplayList(addr[(index-1)*4 + rearDirection])
    G_NOOP 0x65

0044 rev12 turns the brackets into a suppressed nested G_DL in the walks the
span does not belong to. The two spans are EXCLUSIVE, never additive: the
four direction variants share the section's own road surface, so drawing both
in one walk is a coplanar double submission -- trap A4's "flat patches &
smears" and stale depth. The eyes run span 1 only and are bit-identical to
1.0.0.12; the rear walk runs span 2 only.

This is NOT trap A3. It does not widen the section window and it is not
RaYRoD's whole-course draw: it is the game's own per-track, per-direction
asset, the one MK64 draws whenever you look behind. No geometry appears that
the game does not already show from that section.

Every risk from the diagnosis is honoured HERE, at the emit site:
  * pathCounter / playerDirection are NOT written by the rear emit --
    draw_transparent_geography and CM_DrawTransparency read both back
    (render_courses.c:198-237). Water and transparent geography stay
    forward-keyed in the pane: a known, documented residual.
  * the already-computed section index is REUSED rather than re-derived, so
    the three `index == 255` / pathCounter fallbacks above cannot produce a
    different (or out-of-table) answer for the rear list than for the
    forward one.
  * Bowser's Castle's credits-quality statue LOD swap is MIRRORED for the
    rear index, evaluated against the rear index exactly as the stock branch
    evaluates it against the forward one.
  * the span is emitted only from `render_track_sections`, so mods' own
    `Track::Draw` (engine/tracks/Track.cpp, which emits every section
    unconditionally) is untouched and cannot double-draw.
  * the rear span is emitted AFTER the forward span, i.e. after all of its
    state, so the wrapper's render-mode/combine/fog reset still closes both.
  * nothing is emitted at all unless the two direction buckets DIFFER, which
    is most of the point: on a straight the pane's list is already right, and
    a span that changed no answer would make `rear_dl_swaps` a lie (trap D32's
    corollary).

`vr set rearsec 0` is the red control (F3).

REV2 (VR R21 item 3, the cinematic cameras): THE SAME HOLE, IN THE EYES. In the
end-of-race results and the title attract demo MK64 runs camera mode 3 -- a
scripted trackside camera (func_8001A588) that cuts between presets along the
path and may follow another kart -- while the VR first-person seat stays in
player 1's kart. render_track_sections picks the section list from the GAME
camera: its section (camera->collision, mode != 1 branch) and its yaw bucket.
So the eyes were handed "section S as seen from the trackside camera, looking
the camera's way" while looking from the kart, down the kart's heading: the
road strip (shared by every direction variant) drew and the ground around it
did not -- the user's results screenshot. Measured in VR-R21-NOTES §3.
Telemetry (every VR frame, both arms): gSohVRCine* -- camera mode and
playerId, the camera's and the seat's yaw buckets, the camera's and player 1's
sections, the index drawn, and how often they disagreed.
gSohVRCineSec (the fix, `vr set cinesec`, ships 1): in a VR FIRST-PERSON world frame
whose camera is a cinematic one (mode 3), the eyes' section and direction come
from player 1's kart -- the seat -- exactly as mode 1 derives them from a
camera sitting behind that kart. Racing (mode 1), the fly-by (TourCamera),
third person / Diorama (seated ON the game camera) and the flat game never take
the branch.


